<main id="main">
<section class="phero"><img class="phero-bg" src="/assets/img/photos/financial-calculator.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/financial-calculator-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/financial-calculator.webp 1200w" sizes="100vw" width="1200" height="749" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" data-zoom><div class="wrap"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><i aria-hidden="true">›</i><span aria-current="page">Claim terms</span></nav><p class="kicker">Reference</p><h1>Insurance Claim Terms Glossary</h1><p class="lede">43 terms you’ll meet in policies, estimates and appraisal awards, defined in plain English. Type to filter.</p></div></section><div class="wrap twocol"><article class="prose"><div class="filter"><label for="gloss-filter">Search the glossary</label><input id="gloss-filter" type="search" placeholder="Try “holdback” or “umpire”" autocomplete="off"><p class="hint" data-gloss-count>43 terms</p></div><div class="az"><a href="#g-A">A</a><a href="#g-B">B</a><a href="#g-C">C</a><a href="#g-D">D</a><a href="#g-E">E</a><a href="#g-G">G</a><a href="#g-H">H</a><a href="#g-I">I</a><a href="#g-L">L</a><a href="#g-M">M</a><a href="#g-O">O</a><a href="#g-P">P</a><a href="#g-R">R</a><a href="#g-S">S</a><a href="#g-T">T</a><a href="#g-U">U</a><a href="#g-W">W</a><a href="#g-X">X</a></div><dl class="glossary"><div class="gterm" id="g-A"><dt>Actual cash value (ACV)</dt><dd>The value of damaged property at the time of loss, usually replacement cost minus depreciation.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Additional living expense (ALE)</dt><dd>Coverage for extra costs of living elsewhere while your home is uninhabitable after a covered loss.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Appraisal clause</dt><dd>The policy condition that lets either party demand appraisal when they disagree on the amount of loss.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Appraisal award</dt><dd>The written decision, signed by any two of the three panel members, that sets the amount of loss.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Appraiser</dt><dd>The person each side names to value the loss on an appraisal panel; usually required to be competent and independent.</dd></div><div class="gterm" id="g-B"><dt>Bad faith</dt><dd>A legal claim that an insurer unreasonably handled or denied a claim. Decided by courts, not appraisal panels.</dd></div><div class="gterm" id="g-C"><dt>Class 4 shingle</dt><dd>A shingle rated for the highest impact resistance under the UL 2218 test; common in hail-prone Wyoming towns.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Collapse</dt><dd>A coverage term, defined in each policy, for the sudden falling in of a building or part of one, such as from snow weight.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Cosmetic damage exclusion</dt><dd>An endorsement that excludes damage that changes appearance but not function, often applied to dented metal roofing.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Coverage A</dt><dd>Dwelling coverage — the limit for the house itself and attached structures.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Coverage B</dt><dd>Other structures coverage for detached garages, shops, barns and fences.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Coverage C</dt><dd>Personal property, or contents, coverage.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Creased shingle</dt><dd>A shingle bent back by wind so that it has lost its seal and much of its wind resistance.</dd></div><div class="gterm" id="g-D"><dt>Declarations page</dt><dd>The summary page of a policy listing limits, deductibles, endorsements and the insured property.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Depreciation</dt><dd>The reduction in value for age, wear and condition, subtracted from replacement cost to reach actual cash value.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Disinterested</dt><dd>Having no financial stake in the outcome; a requirement many policies place on appraisers.</dd></div><div class="gterm" id="g-E"><dt>Endorsement</dt><dd>A form that adds to, removes or changes the terms of a base policy.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Estimate review</dt><dd>A line-by-line check of an insurance estimate for missing items, measurement errors and pricing issues.</dd></div><div class="gterm" id="g-G"><dt>Ground snow load</dt><dd>The design weight of snow on the ground at a location, used by building codes to set roof load requirements.</dd></div><div class="gterm" id="g-H"><dt>Holdback</dt><dd>Recoverable depreciation withheld from the first payment until repairs are completed.</dd></div><div class="gterm" id="g-I"><dt>Ice dam</dt><dd>A ridge of ice at the eaves that traps meltwater, which can back up under shingles and leak inside.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Ice and water shield</dt><dd>A self-adhering waterproof underlayment installed at eaves and valleys, often required by code in snowy areas.</dd></div><div class="gterm" id="g-L"><dt>Line item</dt><dd>A single priced entry in an estimate, such as a quantity of shingles or a square foot of drywall.</dd></div><div class="gterm" id="g-M"><dt>Matching</dt><dd>The question of whether replacement materials must reasonably match undamaged materials in color and style.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Mitigation</dt><dd>Reasonable steps to prevent further damage after a loss, like tarping a roof or extracting water.</dd></div><div class="gterm" id="g-O"><dt>Ordinance or law coverage</dt><dd>Coverage for extra costs to bring repaired portions of a building up to current code.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Overhead and profit (O&amp;P)</dt><dd>A general contractor’s charge, often 10% plus 10%, for coordinating multiple trades on a repair.</dd></div><div class="gterm" id="g-P"><dt>Percentage deductible</dt><dd>A deductible calculated as a percentage of Coverage A rather than a flat dollar amount; common for wind and hail.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Pitch</dt><dd>The steepness of a roof, expressed as inches of rise per 12 inches of run, such as 6/12.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Proof of loss</dt><dd>A sworn statement of the amount claimed, which an insurer may require within a set time after requesting it.</dd></div><div class="gterm" id="g-R"><dt>Recoverable depreciation</dt><dd>Depreciation that can be collected after repairs are completed under a replacement cost policy.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Replacement cost value (RCV)</dt><dd>The cost to repair or replace damaged property with materials of like kind and quality, without deduction for depreciation.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Reservation of rights</dt><dd>A letter in which an insurer continues to handle a claim while reserving the right to deny coverage later.</dd></div><div class="gterm" id="g-S"><dt>Scope of loss</dt><dd>The full list of damaged items and the work needed to repair them.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Square</dt><dd>A roofing unit equal to 100 square feet of roof surface.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Steep charge</dt><dd>An estimate line adding labor cost for roofs too steep to walk safely, usually 7/12 pitch and above.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Suit limitation</dt><dd>The policy condition setting how long you have to file a lawsuit against the insurer.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Supplement</dt><dd>A request to add missing or underpriced items to an existing insurance estimate.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Surplus lines</dt><dd>Coverage placed with insurers not licensed as admitted carriers in a state, used for risks standard insurers won’t write.</dd></div><div class="gterm" id="g-T"><dt>Test square</dt><dd>A 10-by-10-foot area marked on a roof slope where hail hits are counted.</dd></div><div class="gterm" id="g-U"><dt>Umpire</dt><dd>The neutral third member of an appraisal panel who decides items the two appraisers can’t agree on.</dd></div><div class="gterm" id="g-W"><dt>Wind-driven hail</dt><dd>Hail carried at an angle by strong wind, which damages siding, windows and windward roof slopes.</dd></div><div class="gterm" id="g-X"><dt>Xactimate</dt><dd>Estimating software widely used by insurers, adjusters and contractors to price property repairs.</dd></div></dl></article><aside class="side"><div class="side-box side-call"><p class="side-t">Talk it through</p><p>The first conversation is free. We’ll tell you honestly whether appraisal fits your claim.</p><a class="side-tel" href="tel:+18445371427">+1 (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-block" href="/talk-to-us/">Send claim details</a></div><div class="side-box"><p class="side-t">Resources</p><ul class="side-list"><li><a href="/appraisal-step-by-step/">Appraisal step by step</a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-answers/">Appraisal answers (FAQ)</a></li><li><a href="/claim-terms/" aria-current="page">Claim terms glossary</a></li><li><a href="/claim-guides/">Claim guides</a></li></ul></div></aside></div>
